# What is published (GitHub Pages) is only what the game needs to RUN:
#   index.html, credits.txt, .nojekyll, src/, lib/, assets/ (the art the game loads + licence texts), music/ (tracks, tracks.txt, files.json),
#   manifest.webmanifest + sw.js (the Home Screen app and the stored music: see src/pwa.js)
# Everything below stays on the author's computer.

# --- the art packs exactly as downloaded, and art that is not used ---------------------------------------------------------------
# (Several of these packs forbid redistributing them as packs, and some came without a licence file.  The game only uses the pieces
#  cut out of them into assets/env/ and assets/sprites/ - see CREDITS.md.)
assets/sprites/source/
# the full-size painted portraits stay on this machine: the game loads the pixelated atlas in assets/portraits/pixel/ (made by tools/pixelate-portraits.ps1)
assets/portraits/*.jpg
assets/source/
assets/archive/

# --- the music list with the Suno prompts: the author's working file.  The game on a static host reads music/tracks.txt instead (the same list without the prompts, made by tools/music-manifest.mjs)
music/TRACKLIST.txt

# --- local play and development tools (not needed to play online) ------------------------------------------------------------
server.js
play.bat
play.ps1
tools/
# listening copies made by tools/humanize-music.mjs (the music with a little imperfection added); nothing here is used by the game until you copy a file into music/
music-humanized/

# --- editor / assistant settings, and general clutter ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# lets the generator tests run under Node (the browser ignores it)
src/package.json

# screenshots made for sharing (not part of the game)
snapshots/

# trailer frames and renders (large, made by tools/trailer)
tools/trailer/frames/
tools/trailer/out/

# the font download itself (the unzipped font and its licence are in assets/fonts/livingstone/)
assets/fonts/livingstone.zip

# the author's working notes on which sounds to find (the sounds themselves are credited in CREDITS.md and credits.txt)
assets/sfx/SFX-LIST.txt
